  "package.json.meta": "fileFormatVersion: 2\nguid: 6eb01f7c94d143d88233a4a0c8d2419d\nTextScriptImporter:\n  externalObjects: {}\n  userData: \n  assetBundleName: \n  assetBundleVariant: \n",
  "README.md": '# Gamealia SDK for Unity (WebGL)\n\nA `.jslib` plugin plus a C# wrapper over the Gamealia JavaScript SDK (`window.Gamealia`). Unity 2021.3 or newer.\n\n## Install\n\n0. Easiest: run `gamealia init` in the Unity project folder. It installs this package as `Packages/com.gamealia.sdk/` and the WebGL template as `Assets/WebGLTemplates/Gamealia/`; then pick the template (step 2) and build. Or by hand:\n1. Copy this folder into your project\'s `Packages/com.gamealia.sdk/` (or add it via Package Manager \u2192 *Add package from disk* \u2192 `package.json`). Copying only `Runtime/` into `Assets/Plugins/Gamealia/` also works.\n2. Your WebGL page must load the SDK **before** the Unity loader. Use the sample template: Package Manager \u2192 Gamealia SDK \u2192 Samples \u2192 *WebGL template* \u2192 Import, move `Gamealia/` to `Assets/WebGLTemplates/Gamealia/`, then pick it in Player Settings \u2192 WebGL \u2192 Resolution and Presentation. With your own template, add this line to its `<head>`:\n\n   ```html\n   <script src="https://gamealia.app/sdk/v1.js"></script>\n   ```\n\n3. Build for WebGL and upload the build folder (its `index.html` at the root).\n\nIn the Editor, on non-WebGL platforms and in a WebGL page that did not load the SDK (e.g. offline), every call works locally: `Init` answers a `"mock"` result, ads answer "not shown", and cloud data is kept in `PlayerPrefs`.\n\n## Usage\n\n```csharp\nGamealia.Init(info => {\n    // info.locale: "es", "en"...; info.environment: "gamealia" | "preview" | "autotest" | "mock"\n    Gamealia.Game.LoadingStop();          // required, once the game is playable\n});\n\nGamealia.Game.GameplayStart();            // around actual play\nGamealia.Game.GameplayStop();\nGamealia.Game.HappyTime();\n\nGamealia.Ad.RequestMidgame(shown => Resume());                          // at natural breaks\nGamealia.Ad.RequestRewarded((shown, rewarded) => { if (rewarded) Give(); });\n```\n\nThe full sample is in `Samples~/Basic/GamealiaSample.cs`.\n\n## API mapping\n\nAll callbacks run on the main thread, asynchronously. They never throw. Failures produce the same fallback values the JS SDK uses.\n\n| C# | JS SDK |\n|---|---|\n| `Gamealia.Init(Action<InitResult>)`, `Gamealia.Info`, `Gamealia.Locale`, `Gamealia.IsMobile` | `init()` |\n| `Gamealia.Game.LoadingStart/LoadingStop/GameplayStart/GameplayStop/HappyTime()` | `game.*` |\n| `Gamealia.Ad.RequestMidgame(Action<bool shown>)` | `ad.requestMidgame()` |\n| `Gamealia.Ad.RequestRewarded(Action<bool shown, bool rewarded>)` | `ad.requestRewarded()` |\n| `Gamealia.User.Get(Action<PublicUser>)`, `GetToken(Action<string>)`, `RequestLogin(Action<PublicUser>)` | `user.get/getToken/requestLogin()` |\n| `Gamealia.Data.Load(Action<LoadResult>)` (`ok`, `json`, `error`) | `data.load()` |\n| `Gamealia.Data.Get<T>/Set<T>` (JsonUtility objects), `GetJson/SetJson`, `GetString/SetString`, `GetInt/SetInt`, `GetFloat/SetFloat`, `GetBool/SetBool`, `Remove`, `Clear` | `data.get/set/remove/clear()` |\n| `Gamealia.Room.GetJoinCode()` (sync), `InviteLink(code, Action<string>)`, `ShowInvite(code)`, `Publish(RoomInfo)`, `Unpublish()` | `room.*` |\n| `Gamealia.Presence.SetStatus(text)` | `presence.setStatus()` |\n| events `OnAdStart`, `OnAdEnd`, `OnPause`, `OnResume`, `OnMute`, `OnUnmute`, `OnUserChange`, `OnRoomJoin` | `on(event)` |\n\n- **Ads**: pause the game until the callback fires. With `Gamealia.AutoMuteAudio` (default `true`), `AudioListener.pause` is set while an ad plays or while the portal asks to mute. Grant rewards only when `rewarded` is true.\n- **Cloud save**: 1 MB per player and game. `Data.Load` returning `ok == false` means the save could not be read, so do not overwrite it.\n- **Locale**: `Gamealia.Locale` is the player\'s language. The game decides how to use it.\n- **Permissions**: camera and microphone access is declared in the game listing on the developer dashboard (the iframe gets the matching `allow`). The game then uses the normal browser and engine APIs. The SDK has no call for this.\n\n## How it works\n\n`Gamealia.jslib` calls `window.Gamealia` and replies with `SendMessage("GamealiaBridge", "OnResult", json)`. Events arrive as `SendMessage("GamealiaBridge", "OnEvent", json)`. The `GamealiaBridge` GameObject is created automatically and survives scene loads. Do not rename or destroy it.\n\n`test/jslib.test.ts` runs the jslib against a fake Unity `Module` and a fake (and the real) `window.Gamealia`: `pnpm -F com.gamealia.sdk test`. Only `package.json`, `README.md`, `Runtime/` and `Samples~/` (see `files`) are part of the Unity package.\n',
