function registerPrompts(server, locale = "en") {
  server.registerPrompt(
    "publish-game",
    { title: "Publish a game on Gamealia", description: "End to end: login, analyze, integrate, build, autotest, listing with cover, upload, submit, track.", argsSchema: args },
    ({ dir = ".", game }) => msg2(`Publish the game in ${dir} on Gamealia, end to end.

${steps([
      "gamealia_whoami; if not logged in, gamealia_login, show the user the URL and code, then gamealia_login {wait:true}.",
      'If the user belongs to several developer accounts (gamealia_whoami says so), gamealia_accounts {action:"list"}, ask which account the game is for and switch to it (gamealia_accounts {action:"switch", account}) before creating or publishing. A role-forbidden error means an owner or admin of the account must act: tell the user, do not retry.',
      `gamealia_analyze_project {dir:"${dir}"}: engine, build command, output dir, SDKs, policy findings. (No game yet? gamealia_create_project first.)`,
      "Fix every policy finding at the file and line given.",
      `gamealia_integrate_sdk {dir:"${dir}"} (dry run), review the diff, then write:true. Place the returned TODOs: gameplayStart/gameplayStop where play starts/stops (gameplayStop is required by the autotest), happyTime on wins, Gamealia.ad.requestMidgame() at natural breaks (pause and mute while it plays).`,
      LOCALE_STEP,
      `gamealia_check_integration {dir:"${dir}"}; fix every FAIL.`,
      "gamealia_build if there is a build step.",
      `gamealia_run_autotest {dir:"${dir}"}; look at the screenshots. Repeat until it passes (fix-autotest-failures prompt if needed).`,
      "Optional: gamealia_playtest / gamealia_playtest_act to play it yourself; gamealia_preview gives the user a URL to try it.",
      `${game ? `gamealia_update_listing {game:"${game}"}` : "gamealia_create_game"}: slug, title/description/controls in es and en (write both), 1-6 category tags plus up to 8 mechanic tags (how it plays) and attribute tags, orientation, multiplayer, adsEnabled.`,
      "Translate the listing yourself into every other supported locale (the status tool with texts:true gives the source text, each locale's status and the limits); keep tone and proper nouns; save all missing and machine locales in one gamealia_update_listing {game, texts}.",
      "gamealia_generate_cover from the desktop-input autotest screenshot, with game set (uploads cover and thumbnail).",
      `gamealia_upload_version {dir:"${dir}", game:"<slug>"}: waits for the server autotest.`,
      "Show the user the result and ask before submitting; then gamealia_submit_for_review with release notes.",
      "gamealia_get_status later: approved = live; rejected = fix each reason, upload and submit again."
    ])}

${policy(locale)}`)
  );
  server.registerPrompt(
    "migrate-from-crazygames",
    { title: "Migrate a CrazyGames game", description: "Swap the CrazyGames SDK for the Gamealia shim, then publish.", argsSchema: args },
    ({ dir = ".", game }) => migrate("CrazyGames", dir, game ?? "", locale)
  );
  server.registerPrompt(
    "migrate-from-poki",
    { title: "Migrate a Poki game", description: "Swap the Poki SDK for the Gamealia shim, then publish.", argsSchema: args },
    ({ dir = ".", game }) => migrate("Poki", dir, game ?? "", locale)
  );
  server.registerPrompt(
    "fix-autotest-failures",
    { title: "Fix autotest failures", description: "Diagnose and fix a failing local or server autotest, then rerun it.", argsSchema: args },
    ({ dir = ".", game }) => msg2(`The Gamealia autotest fails for the game in ${dir}. Fix it.

${steps([
      `${game ? `gamealia_get_status {game:"${game}"} for the server report, and ` : ""}gamealia_run_autotest {dir:"${dir}"} to reproduce locally. Read failedRequired, each problem's fix, the console errors, and look at the screenshots.`,
      "For each failing check, read its entry in gamealia://docs/en-autotest-checks (or gamealia_docs_search with the check id).",
      'Typical fixes: sdk_loaded -> gamealia_integrate_sdk; sdk_init -> call Gamealia.init() first; locale -> pick the UI language from Gamealia.init().locale (or peekInit().locale), falling back to the closest language the game has, and follow Gamealia.on("localeChange"); loading_stop -> call Gamealia.game.loadingStop() when ready; not_blank -> draw something within 5 s (a background and a title in index.html with inline styles show while scripts load; the test frame is black); missing_assets -> fix paths (case-sensitive) or include the files; security checks -> remove the code at the file:line given; undeclared hosts -> declare backendHosts in the listing.',
      "Use gamealia_playtest + gamealia_playtest_act to see what the game does after input when the cause is unclear; gamealia_preview shows the console in a real browser for the user.",
      "Edit the code, gamealia_build if needed, then gamealia_run_autotest again. Repeat until status is pass (or only warnings remain).",
      game ? `gamealia_upload_version {dir:"${dir}", game:"${game}"} and then gamealia_submit_for_review once the user confirms.` : "Continue with the publish-game workflow (listing, upload, submit)."
    ])}

Do not weaken checks or hide errors (e.g. by swallowing exceptions or faking SDK calls): fix the cause.

${policy(locale)}`)
  );
}

