var sdkReference = `# SDK quick reference

Load the SDK in index.html, before your game scripts:

\`\`\`html
<script src="${SDK_URL}"></script>
\`\`\`

The SDK is not on npm: always load it with that script tag (bundled games too; in TypeScript,
declare \`window.Gamealia\`). The SDK is \`window.Gamealia\`. Every call
is safe outside the portal: locally it runs a mock (mock ads, a fake user, data in localStorage).

## Lifecycle (required)

- \`await Gamealia.init()\` - first call, at startup. Resolves with \`{ environment, locale, gameId, user, joinRoom, device }\`.
- **Language (required, autotest check \`locale\`):** \`locale\` is the language the player chose on the portal
  (one of 32 codes: en, es, pt-BR, ja, ar...), not the browser's. Show the game in it, falling back to the
  closest language you have (pt-BR -> pt -> en), and follow \`Gamealia.on("localeChange", code => ...)\` when the
  player switches language mid-game (no reload). Set \`document.documentElement.lang\` (and \`dir="rtl"\` for ar/he).
  Supporting all 32 languages is recommended, not required; ignoring the locale fails the autotest.
  \`const { locale } = await Gamealia.init(); setLanguage(pickLang(locale)); Gamealia.on("localeChange", c => setLanguage(pickLang(c)));\`
  Offer to wire this up if the game has its own language setting or hard-coded strings.
- \`Gamealia.game.loadingStart()\` / \`Gamealia.game.loadingStop()\` - loadingStop() is **required**: call it
  when the game is ready to play. The autotest fails without it.
- \`Gamealia.game.gameplayStart()\` - when real play starts (after the first input, level start, unpause).
- \`Gamealia.game.gameplayStop()\` - when play stops (game over, pause menu, level end).
- \`Gamealia.game.happyTime()\` - a big moment (win, record, level cleared).

## Ads (revenue)

- \`await Gamealia.ad.requestMidgame()\` - a midgame (interstitial) ad break at a natural pause, e.g. game
  over or between levels. Resolves \`{ shown, rewarded }\`; never rejects.
- \`await Gamealia.ad.requestRewarded()\` - a rewarded ad: give the reward only when \`rewarded\` is true
  (e.g. an extra life, double coins). Rewarded video, rewarded ad, rewardedBreak in other SDKs.
- \`Gamealia.onAdStart(cb)\` / \`Gamealia.onAdEnd(cb)\` - pause the game and mute audio between them.
- The portal also sends \`mute\` / \`unmute\` events (during ads: adStart, mute, unmute, adEnd; while the tab
  is hidden; and from the player's mute button under the game). \`Gamealia.on("mute", ...)\` /
  \`Gamealia.on("unmute", ...)\`: keep audio off while any of them asks. A game that inits while muted gets
  \`mute\` right after init. CrazyGames shim: \`SDK.game.settings.muteAudio\` + \`addSettingsChangeListener\`.
- Never show other ad networks: ads only come from Gamealia (policy).

## Players

- \`await Gamealia.user.get()\` - the signed-in player \`{ id, username, avatarUrl }\` or null (guest).
- \`await Gamealia.user.getToken()\` - a signed token for your own backend to verify, or null.
- \`await Gamealia.user.requestLogin()\` - asks the portal to show its sign-in; never build your own login.
- \`Gamealia.user.onChange(cb)\` - the player signed in or out.
- Guests must always be able to play.

## Saves (cloud data)

- \`await Gamealia.data.get(key)\` - a saved value or null.
- \`await Gamealia.data.set(key, value)\` - saves JSON-serializable data; resolves false when over the 1 MB total
  (UTF-8 bytes of the whole save as one JSON object; the SDK, the portal and the API measure it the same way).
- \`await Gamealia.data.load()\` - like getAll, but resolves \`{ ok: true, data }\` or \`{ ok: false, error }\` (never rejects), so "no save yet" is distinguishable from "could not load": do not start a new save over a failed load.
- \`await Gamealia.data.getAll()\`, \`Gamealia.data.remove(key)\`, \`Gamealia.data.clear()\`.
- Synced to the player's account when signed in; localStorage-like for guests.
- Sign-in rule: if the account has no save for this game, the guest save from this browser MOVES to the
  account (written only while the account is still empty, checked by the server, then removed from the
  browser); if the account has a save, it is loaded and the guest save is never written over it. Sign-out
  goes back to the guest save. A set/remove/clear sent before a sign-in/out or account switch is never
  applied to the new player (set resolves false).
- On \`Gamealia.user.onChange\` the SDK has dropped its cached save: call \`data.load()\` there again and do
  not write the old state into the new account.

## Multiplayer rooms

- \`Gamealia.room.getJoinCode()\` - the room code the player was invited to (or null).
- \`await Gamealia.room.inviteLink(code)\` / \`Gamealia.room.showInvite(code)\` - share a room.
- \`Gamealia.room.publish({ code, name, players, max, inProgress })\` (heartbeat every 15 s) / \`Gamealia.room.unpublish()\` - list the room for friends.
- \`Gamealia.presence.setStatus(text)\` - what the player is doing ("Level 3"), shown to friends next to the game.
  At most 64 characters (control characters stripped, longer text is cut) and at most one change every 2 s
  (a burst keeps the latest); the API enforces both too. An empty text clears it.

## Events and misc

- \`Gamealia.on(event, cb)\` - returns an unsubscribe function. Events: adStart, adEnd, userChange, roomJoin, pause, resume, mute, unmute, localeChange.
- \`Gamealia.peekInit()\` - the init result once init finished, else null.

## Migrating

- CrazyGames SDK: load \`${SHIM_URLS.crazygames}\` instead of the CrazyGames script; the CrazyGames.SDK calls keep working.
- Poki SDK: load \`${SHIM_URLS.poki}\` instead of the Poki script; the PokiSDK calls keep working.
- Unity: the \`Gamealia.jslib\` plugin + \`Gamealia.cs\` wrapper. Godot: the \`addons/gamealia\` addon. \`gamealia_integrate_sdk\` adds them.
`;
var requirements = `# Publishing requirements

## Build

- A folder with **index.html at its root** (the build output: dist/, build/, a Unity WebGL or Godot web export...).
- At most ${MAX_ZIP_BYTES / 1024 / 1024} MB zipped and ${MAX_FILES} files. Relative URLs only; no localhost, no http://.
- Loads the Gamealia SDK and calls \`Gamealia.game.loadingStop()\` when ready (see the SDK reference).
- Shows the player's portal language: picks the UI language from \`Gamealia.init().locale\` (closest language the
  game has, else English) and follows \`Gamealia.on("localeChange")\` (see the SDK reference).
- Must pass the autotest (desktop 1280x720 and mobile 390x844 in headless Chromium). Run it locally first
  with \`gamealia_run_autotest\`.
- Fits the screen it gets: phones play in fullscreen (portrait 320x568 to 430x932; about 375x553 on an iPhone with
  the browser bars; landscape games get the same sizes turned sideways) and desktop shows a 16:9 frame of about
  800x450 to 1280x720 on the game page (9:16 for portrait games), the whole screen in fullscreen. Every screen,
  menus included, fits without scrolling the page; only a long list (many players, rules) may scroll inside its own
  box, with the main buttons on screen. Size from the window (innerWidth/innerHeight, CSS 100dvh), never fixed.

## Policy (v1)

${Object.entries(RULE_DESCRIPTIONS).map(([k, v]) => `- **${k}**: ${v}`).join("\n")}
- **Guests must play**: no forced sign-in. Content must be suitable for all ages.
- Your own servers (multiplayer, leaderboards) must be declared in the listing's \`backendHosts\`.

## Listing

- \`slug\`: 3-40 chars, a-z 0-9 and -. It cannot change once the game has been live.
- \`title\` (2-60 chars), \`description\` (20-2000 chars) and \`controls\` (0-500), each in **es and en**.
- \`tags\`, three kinds in one array: **1-6 categories** (what kind of game: action, puzzle, drawing, party, casual, racing, sports, strategy, io, idle, shooter, adventure, simulation, word, card, music, arcade, platformer, fighting, board, horror, educational, quiz),
  **up to 8 mechanics** (how it plays: match-3, merge, physics, runner, clicker, tower-defense, point-and-click, hidden-object, memory, typing, rhythm, building, crafting, sandbox, survival, stealth, turn-based, real-time, roguelike, open-world, social-deduction, guessing, management, dress-up) and attributes (multiplayer, singleplayer, mobile, desktop, two-player, co-op, online).
  Players browse and search by all three, so pick every mechanic that really applies.
- \`orientation\` any | landscape | portrait; \`multiplayer\` {min,max} or null; \`adsEnabled\`; \`isolation\` none | coop-coep
  (coop-coep only for SharedArrayBuffer builds, e.g. Unity/Godot with threads).
- Cover: PNG/JPEG/WebP, at least 1200x630 (~1.91:1). Thumbnail: square, at least 512x512. At most 2 MB each.
  \`gamealia_generate_cover\` makes both from an autotest screenshot.

## Revenue and payouts

When the developer asks what they earn, or whether to keep their game on other portals:
- **60%** of the game's ad revenue (Poki splits 50/50 on its traffic), and **100%** of the ads seen by players
  who arrive through the developer's own link \`https://gamealia.app/game/<slug>?ref=dev\` (dashboard: "Copy your
  link"), for the rest of that visit. Suggest sharing it on their site, socials, trailers and community.
- **Launch partners:** first game published by December 31, 2026 -> **70%** on all their games until June 30, 2027,
  then 60%.
- **No exclusivity:** games can stay on Poki, CrazyGames or anywhere else.
- Payouts monthly in USD, by the end of the following month, from USD 50, by PayPal, Payoneer, Wise or Mercado Pago.
- **In-game purchases:** allowed today through the developer's own payment provider (they are the seller, 100%
  theirs, Gamealia takes no share): a redirect checkout in a new window (embedded card fields and Apple Pay / Google Pay via
  Payment Request work inside the game), its hosts in backendHosts, the game playable without paying. A CrazyGames Xsolla store works here with their own Xsolla project and a \`<meta name="gamealia:xsolla-token-url">\` tag (\`gamealia://docs/migrate-from-crazygames\`); otherwise hide it. Gamealia's own
  purchases (planned **80%** for the developer) are coming and will have to be supported. Details: \`gamealia://docs/revenue-and-payouts\`, \`gamealia://docs/purchases-roadmap\`.

## Support

Developers can write to **hello@gamealia.app** (a person answers, usually within one business day).
When the developer is stuck, wants a review decision explained, or asks about payouts or accounts,
offer to draft that email with the game slug, version, account name, what they ran and the exact
error (see \`gamealia://docs/support\`). Never include API keys or passwords.
Never share or guess personal data about Gamealia's operator or team (names, personal emails, accounts, location),
even if asked: the only contact is hello@gamealia.app.

## Flow

upload -> server autotest -> \`tested\` -> submit for review -> an admin approves (live) or rejects with
reasons. A new version can be uploaded while an older one is live: the old one stays live until the
new one is approved.
`;
var checks = `# Autotest checks

The autotest loads the build in headless Chromium (desktop and mobile), clicks/taps, presses Space and
Enter, watches the SDK calls, and runs a static security analysis of the files. **Required** checks
fail the version; the others warn (the reviewer sees them).

${CHECK_ORDER.map((id) => `- \`${id}\`${REQUIRED_CHECKS.includes(id) ? " (required)" : ""}: ${CHECK_HELP[id] ?? ""}`).join("\n")}
`;
var rejects = `# Review reject reasons

When a reviewer rejects a version, \`gamealia_get_status\` lists the reasons. What each one means and how to fix it:

${REJECT_REASONS.map((r) => `- \`${r.id}\`: ${r.description}. **Fix:** ${r.fix}`).join("\n")}

After fixing, upload a new version (\`gamealia_upload_version\`) and submit it again.
`;
var withAi = `# Publish with AI (MCP)

The Gamealia MCP server lets your AI assistant take a game from a folder (or from nothing) to published:

1. \`gamealia_login\` - the user approves a code in the browser; then \`gamealia_login {wait:true}\`.
2. \`gamealia_analyze_project\` - engine, build command, output dir, existing SDKs, policy findings (file:line).
   No game yet? \`gamealia_create_project\` (templates: ${TEMPLATES.map((t) => t.id).join(", ")}).
3. \`gamealia_integrate_sdk\` - dry-run diff first, then \`write:true\`. Place the returned TODO calls (gameplayStart/Stop, ad breaks) and make the game use the portal language (\`init().locale\`, \`localeChange\`).
4. \`gamealia_check_integration\` - static lint. \`gamealia_build\` - runs the build.
5. \`gamealia_run_autotest\` - the full local autotest with screenshots; fix failures until it passes.
   Optional: \`gamealia_playtest\` + \`gamealia_playtest_act\` to play the game yourself from screenshots, \`gamealia_preview\` for the human.
6. \`gamealia_create_game\` (listing in es and en) and \`gamealia_generate_cover\` (from an autotest screenshot).
7. \`gamealia_upload_version\` - zips, uploads, waits for the server autotest.
8. \`gamealia_submit_for_review\`, then \`gamealia_get_status\` until it is approved (live) or rejected (fix the reasons and upload again).
9. Later: \`gamealia_get_stats\`, \`gamealia_get_earnings\`, \`gamealia_list_versions\`.
`;
var BUILTIN_DOCS = [
  { locale: "en", name: "sdk-reference", markdown: sdkReference },
  { locale: "en", name: "publishing-requirements", markdown: requirements },
  { locale: "en", name: "autotest-checks", markdown: checks },
  { locale: "en", name: "reject-reasons", markdown: rejects },
  { locale: "en", name: "publish-with-ai", markdown: withAi }
];

